● Frontend review: apps/nextjs-app (branch dev @ d529dd7)

  The frontend has real security holes. I found three High-severity script-execution or data-leak bugs and a set of Medium configuration problems. Two of
  the High ones are in code this fork added (the graph tooltip XSS and the AI-chat state bleed between bases); the rest are inherited from upstream Teable
  but still live in this deployment.

  Scope. I reviewed the whole Next.js app. I went deepest on the roughly 22k lines added since the Teable import (fd44761), and a separate pass swept the
  whole app for security. I confirmed every High and the most important Medium findings against the source myself. The structure and bug findings come from
  four parallel reviewers, each told to read the code and drop anything it couldn't confirm. Paths are relative to apps/nextjs-app/src/ unless they start
  with apps/. [fork] marks code this repo added; [upstream] marks code inherited from Teable that is still live here.

