  The intended principles are sound: thin pages, feature-sliced blocks, an SDK as the single way to the backend, pure functions tested apart from the UI,
  and URL state for anything shareable. The newer fork code (base-graph, schema-onboarding, email) mostly follows them, with good pure/UI separation and
  spec coverage.

  1.2 Where the structure breaks down

  1. A second, unused design system [fork].
     - components/ui/* is a second shadcn set. It is used only by components/ai-elements and one file, auth/DescContent.tsx.
     - Of the 25 vendored ai-elements files, 19 (about 3.3k lines) are never imported, including agent, artifact, canvas, sandbox, terminal, open-in-chat
       and voice-selector.
     - Its styles have drifted from ui-lib (for example, Button has no xs size and no dark variants), so the chat panel mixes two looks.
     - It also pulls in heavy dependencies (@xyflow/react, media-chrome, shiki, tokenlens).
     - Fix: point the 6 used ai-elements at @teable/ui-lib/shadcn, then delete components/ui and the unused elements.
  2. Bypassing the import alias. chat-panel/* imports '../../../../../../components/ai-elements/...' (6 levels up) instead of @/components/....
  3. Dependencies pointing the wrong way.
     - components/setting/integration imports ImapConnectForm from blocks/email, so a shared component depends on a feature block.
     - components/* imports from features/* (TeableLogo, Guide, ChangelogNotification).
     - Fix: move shared pieces down a layer.
  4. Duplicated logic.
     - There are two OAuth launchers: useOAuthPopup and openConnectIntegration. The second sends callBackType/integrationId, which the backend ignores.
     - maskEmail exists on both client and server.
     - The metadata-email cast is copied twice.
  5. Oversized files. 22 files exceed the project's 500-line rule.
     - The fork-added ones are ChatPanel.tsx (711), prompt-input.tsx (1314) and code-block.tsx (523).
     - ChatPanel.tsx mixes upload, streaming, persistence, selection-to-context and layout. Split it into useChatStream, useChatUpload, useChatPersistence
       and useSelectionContext.
  6. A 704 KB static bundle. features/help/helpPages.ts is HTML scraped from help.teable.ai and statically imported by BaseLayout, so it ships in every base
     page's JavaScript. Load it lazily or fetch it as JSON.
  7. Query-key discipline. New code mostly uses inline keys (['email-sources', baseId], ['base-usage', baseId]), so cross-feature invalidation gets missed.
     Examples: deleting an integration doesn't refresh email status, and installing packs doesn't refresh the graph schema. Register them in ReactQueryKeys.
  8. Committed tooling files [fork].
     - 9 .claude-flow/data/pending-insights.jsonl files sit inside src/ and leak /home/avarile/... paths.
     - Also committed: msapplication-icon-144x144 copy.png, babel.config.backup.js and .idea/*.
     - Fix: remove them and add .claude-flow/ to .gitignore and .dockerignore.
  9. Test gaps. No specs cover the code where the bugs below are: ChatPanel, both graph canvases, ai-context.utils.ts (pure, 347 lines), graphTheme.ts, the
     help feature, and the email dialogs.
  10. i18n leaks.
      - 41 ai.chat.*/ai.files.* keys are missing in every locale except en and zh.
      - admin.setting.ai.* keys are missing even in en and zh.
      - Hardcoded English appears in HelpModal, GraphQueryPanel ("OK"), preset labels and APIDialogContent ("Token").

