  3. Security

  High

  #: S1
  Where: features/app/blocks/base-graph/BaseGraphCanvas.tsx:395/405 and BaseGraphCanvas2D.tsx:449/459 [fork]
  Issue: Stored XSS. nodeLabel returns the raw primary-field value. float-tooltip@1.7.5 renders string content with .html(), which I confirmed in its dist
  file, and the backend's labelOf doesn't escape.                             
  Exploit: An editor sets a record's primary value to <img src=x onerror=…>. Any collaborator who hovers that node in the graph runs the script in their own

  session.
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: S2
  Where: features/app/components/notifications/notification-component/LinkNotification.tsx:60,68 [upstream]
  Issue: Stored XSS. The notification text is rendered with dangerouslySetInnerHTML. i18next escaping is off: the block in next-i18next.config.js:43-47 is
  commented out, so the default escapeValue:false applies. The substituted values (fromUserName, fieldName, tableName) are free text.
  Exploit: A collaborator renames a field to an HTML payload, then mentions the victim. The script runs when the victim opens their notifications.
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: S3
  Where: features/app/components/plugin/hooks/iframe-url/* and IframePluginRender.tsx:71 [upstream]
  Issue: Plugin URL allows javascript:. There's no protocol allow-list on create or update, no sandbox on the iframe, and any logged-in user can create and
  install their own plugin.
  Exploit: A javascript:fetch('/api/…')// plugin on a dashboard runs in the parent origin for every member, and for anonymous share viewers too.
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: S4
  Where: apps/nestjs-backend/src/features/share/share.service.ts:255 [upstream, backend]
  Issue: Hidden-field leak on share links. projection: query?.projection ?? visibleFields trusts the caller, and filter can be overridden the same way.
  Hidden field IDs are exposed in view.columnMeta, including in __NEXT_DATA__.
  Exploit: Anyone with the share link calls GET /api/share/{id}/view/records?projection[]=fldHidden and gets the hidden column's values.

  Medium

  #: S5
  Where: pages/base/[baseId]/[[...slug]].tsx:51, all pages/share/**, share-base-ssr.ts:84             
  Issue: setHeader('Content-Security-Policy', 'frame-ancestors *;') replaces the entire CSP. The main logged-in app page therefore runs with no script-src
  (so nothing blocks S1–S3) and can be framed by any site, with X-Frame-Options ignored. The session cookie also has no explicit SameSite.
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  #: S6 
  Where: apps/nextjs-app/next.config.js:78-110           
  Issue: Where the CSP does apply, it is weak: 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval', upstream *.teable.io/.ai/.cn script hosts this deployment doesn't control,
  frame-src *, and img-src of any http/https. There's no Permissions-Policy even though voice input uses the microphone, and HSTS lasts 4 days. As a side
  effect, GA and a custom UMAMI_URL are blocked by the CSP.
  ────────────────────────────────────────               
